From 04af33abed5e7368050b9374d74e82c8aef546b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:44:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 63/67] contrib: bluray: 1.5.0 with SamuriHL's libbluray fixes
 (menus, BD-J, seeks)

libbluray 1.5.0 (from 1.4.1) with the fixes SamuriHL keeps for CoreELEC's Kodi
(github.com/SamuriHL/CoreELEC, packages/multimedia/libbluray/patches):
HDMV menus (the BC compare, button programs ending at a link command,
always-on pages, cleared planes flushed at a page change, composition
crops), BD-J (screen configuration matching, xlets stopped in order,
present xlets left unloaded until started, selectLanguage, the JVM run
with -Xrs so it leaves the signals to the player - here Android's ART in
the same process), seeks (limited to the title, the starting packet kept,
the end of a playlist raised again), the playitem connection condition
and the clip infos exposed, 3D subtitle depth info, 2160p video size.

Left out: the Kodi tmpdir (1.5.0 already runs AWT not headless), the
BD-J background plane (a third overlay plane the player must draw) and
the presentation timing (opt-in, driven by the player); 40 and 44 taken
without the context of those. download.videolan.org publishes no
checksum for 1.5.0: SHA512SUMS has the one of the tarball used.

Message-Id: <20261123-contrib-bluray-samurihl@djnice>
